# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles MUST keep LF in the working tree, even on Windows.
# With core.autocrlf=true and no rule, a fresh Windows clone checks these out as
# CRLF. A CRLF shell script fails to run on Linux/WSL/CI — the kernel tries to
# exec the interpreter from the shebang as `/usr/bin/env bash\r` (or breaks a
# Docker entrypoint with "exec ...: No such file or directory", exit 127).
# Scoped to these globs only, so other files keep their platform-native endings.
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
# The systemd unit and launchd plist templates scripts/install.sh renders on Linux and macOS.
scripts/shared/*.template text eol=lf

# Vendored sqlite-vec native libraries (scripts/update-sqlite-vec.ps1): never touch line endings.
*.dll   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
